    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 830,
      "versionNonce": 1527351348,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "5olFWBGYWPAWoyBeFsBpU",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1544.2611199132841,
      "y": 2094.341621319412,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 2695.3125,
      "height": 120,
      "seed": 1735142284,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790483167003,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "text": "For scale:  1. we first shard the redis and db based on geolocation as people are more likely to book event near them.\n            2. we keep multiple redis clustres that are consistently hashed based on event id so one event stays on single redis instance. We also keep multiple instances of our GetEventService and bookingservice behind our gateay\n            3. have multiple layers of check/lock like updating our quries to have where clauses to check if the seat is not booked when already payment done.\n               checking this before payment also. basically have Pessimistic Locking major event. \n            4. for better reads, we will keep event details in redis cache so we minimise reads on our db. ",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "For scale:  1. we first shard the redis and db based on geolocation as people are more likely to book event near them.\n            2. we keep multiple redis clustres that are consistently hashed based on event id so one event stays on single redis instance. We also keep multiple instances of our GetEventService and bookingservice behind our gateay\n            3. have multiple layers of check/lock like updating our quries to have where clauses to check if the seat is not booked when already payment done.\n               checking this before payment also. basically have Pessimistic Locking major event. \n            4. for better reads, we will keep event details in redis cache so we minimise reads on our db. ",
      "lineHeight": 1.2,
      "baseline": 115
    },
